00:07:38.789 --> 00:07:42.590
(ominous music)

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:46.920
In the Halloween episode, we see an angel and a&nbsp;
devil trick-or-treating together, which I see as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:51.240
a foreshadowing of the good and evil metaphor that&nbsp;
comes up so often during this season. We already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:55.500
know about Nica and Chucky, a good character and&nbsp;
an evil character being forced to share one body.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:59.760
Something similar appears to happen after Jake&nbsp;
and Devon capture a Chucky scout and attempt to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:03.840
reprogram his brain. Chucky pretends that he’s&nbsp;
torn between “good Chucky” and “bad Chucky”.

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:08.220
Due to the religious setting, Chucky is constantly&nbsp;
portrayed as The Devil, and they even perform an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:12.180
exorcism on him at the end. When Jake and Devon&nbsp;
first show up to Lexy’s house, she’s listening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:16.920
to the song “Devil I Know” by Allie X, and this&nbsp;
also foreshadows the exorcism of Chucky. Contrary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:21.420
to that, newcomer Nadine is the angel. Chucky&nbsp;
takes her out by stating that fairies love to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:25.320
fly before throwing her out a window, but she&nbsp;
comes back to speak to Lexy in the form of an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:30.000
angel… which is actually just a suit with lights,&nbsp;
but I’m not here to talk about the costume budget.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.720
In addition to the contrast shown between&nbsp;
good and evil, the show also explores the gray&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:38.160
area in between the two, with many good characters&nbsp;
expressing feelings of guilt. We get to see how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:42.360
each of them deals with guilt differently.&nbsp;
The first is actually Lexy’s mom, Mrs. Cross.

00:08:43.353 --> 00:08:48.180
– For everyone who lost somebody in last year's&nbsp;
tragic events, I know exactly what they're going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:57.120
through because I'm going through it too. The&nbsp;
grief. The anger. The guilt. The survivors' guilt.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:01.380
– It’s not known how much she really struggles with&nbsp;
guilt, considering most of what she does is faked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:05.940
for social media, but we see survivors’ guilt&nbsp;
manifest much more convincingly in Jake. During&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:09.960
an art history class about the seven deadly sins,&nbsp;
he asks his teacher if there are some sins that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:13.801
are unforgivable, still shaken by the fact that&nbsp;
his innocent foster brother lost his life due to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.801 --> 00:09:15.452
Jake’s connection with Chucky.

00:09:15.752 --> 00:09:18.578
In a later class,&nbsp;
that teacher senses the guilt eating at him.

00:09:18.937 --> 00:09:21.335
– You think I’m overcome with guilt?

00:09:21.704 --> 00:09:24.369
–I think something’s eating away at you.

00:09:24.369 --> 00:09:27.360
– And sure enough, Jake’s guilt&nbsp;
ties back into the main plot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:29.580
it’s the reason that he wants&nbsp;
to keep Scout Chucky alive.

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:34.500
– I need to try and do it a different&nbsp;
way. All I feel is guilt...&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:39.900
If I really want to forgive myself, I&nbsp;
have to be able to forgive him first.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:44.520
– Nadine has a different relationship with&nbsp;
guilt. She feels guilt over her bad habit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:48.540
with stealing things, but unlike Jake, she’s a&nbsp;
little too comfortable with letting go of it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:52.140
As long as she declares her sins in the&nbsp;
confessional, it all goes away, so she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:56.100
often ends up with long sessions in the booth,&nbsp;
completely missing the point of why she’s there.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:58.740
However, this makes her a&nbsp;
perfect companion to Lexy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:03.060
who keeps all of her guilt bottled up inside.&nbsp;
Through her final conversation with Angel Nadine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:05.820
she’s finally able to share&nbsp;
her feelings with those she loves.

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:07.740
Devon, on the other hand, tries to deal with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:10.560
guilt by physically overcoming&nbsp;
it, seeing it as a sickness.

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:13.560
– [Bryce] I thought you were sick. You shouldn’t&nbsp;
be out of bed if that’s the case.&nbsp;

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:17.340
– [Devon] Maybe it’s just something I ate.
– Or maybe the feeling isn’t biological.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:21.540
Maybe it’s more philosophical. Guilt.&nbsp;
It has a funny way of manifesting in us.

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:25.200
– The point is that each character has&nbsp;
their own way of handling guilt. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:28.800
protagonists find a way to handle it, while&nbsp;
the antagonists make no attempt to address it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:31.920
which all comes to a head before the&nbsp;
exorcism, where each of them must make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:35.520
their confessions in order to proceed. It’s&nbsp;
probably the most well written though line&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:39.649
in the season. I wish I could say the same&nbsp;
about how Dr. Mixter’s character was set up.

00:10:39.751 --> 00:10:44.000
– [Lexy] Our family therapist can't be in league with 
a supernaturally possessed doll, right? RIGHT?

00:10:45.104 --> 00:10:45.780
RIGHT?

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:50.040
– By the way, in Lexy’s room, there’a a Blue Öyster&nbsp;
Cult poster, a reference to her singing their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:53.940
song, “(Don’t Fear) The Reaper” to Caroline&nbsp;
as a lullaby in Season 1. Another Season 1&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:58.440
connection can be seen in this guy, James. He’s&nbsp;
interviewing Mrs. Cross, and he’s actually the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:01.860
same guy that interviewed her when she was&nbsp;
mayor throughout Season 1. Crazy how no one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:05.520
in the media is putting together that the Chucky&nbsp;
doll is attached to so many of these tragedies.

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:09.960
After a family therapy sesh, Dr. Mixter gives&nbsp;
Caroline a new doll to help her cope with her fear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:14.340
of dolls. This is kind of a callback to the 7th&nbsp;
movie, Cult of Chucky, where Tiffany claims that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:19.080
this Good Guy doll was used to help Alice Pierce&nbsp;
overcome her family’s Chucky related tragedy.

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:22.740
Anyway, when it comes to Caroline’s doll,&nbsp;
Lexy smashes it against the ground to try&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:26.220
to make sure it isn’t alive, and we see&nbsp;
the same camera angle used when Junior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:30.420
used Chucky as a blunt object to attack&nbsp;
his dad with last season. This could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:34.080
a tiny clue that this Wedding Belle&nbsp;
doll is actually Chucky in disguise.

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:37.020
Lexy’s precautions don’t save her&nbsp;
from being targeted by Chucky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.020 --> 00:11:40.620
who brings a homemade bomb and detonates&nbsp;
it on Jake’s young foster brother, Gary.

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:45.120
Knowing the truth won’t be believed, they make&nbsp;
up a story about how they built a homemade bomb&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:49.380
which was accidentally detonated. This is&nbsp;
what lands them in the Catholic school. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:53.460
get why they don’t want Chucky being alive to&nbsp;
be part of their story, but their cover story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:56.940
that they made the bomb themselves doesn’t&nbsp;
make them look any better. This is so stupid.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:00.180
They find themselves being transported to&nbsp;
the Catholic School in a blue school bus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:03.960
kind of reminiscent of Andy being shipped&nbsp;
to the military school in Child’s Play 3.

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:07.440
Season 2 Episode 2, “The Sinners Are&nbsp;
Much More Fun” is titled after a lyric&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:09.660
from the Billy Joel song,&nbsp;
“Only the Good Die Young”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:14.220
and opens with some franchise easter eggs&nbsp;
in Jennifer / Tiffany’s house. There’s a never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:17.640
before seen photo from Glen and Glenda’s&nbsp;
5th birthday party in Seed of Chucky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:21.960
which sits alongside Jennifer’s most improved&nbsp;
actress award, also from Seed. In that film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:26.760
it was used by Tiffany to knock out Redman, and&nbsp;
in this season, Glenda uses it to knock out Glen.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:31.380
Moving on through the house, Tiffany has a huge&nbsp;
mirror above her bed, and when she wakes up screaming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:34.860
it begins to crack. It wouldn’t be the&nbsp;
first time she cracked a ceiling mirror,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:37.800
because in Bride of Chucky, two of&nbsp;
her kills come as the result of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:40.560
champagne bottle hurled at the&nbsp;
mirror above a bed at a motel.

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:43.560
Back at the school, Jake, Devon and&nbsp;
Lexy are sitting in on their first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:46.980
homily with the headmaster, Father&nbsp;
Bryce, who loves using metaphors.

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:51.120
–On God’s team, every confession is a victory… And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:54.553
God sure does love a winner.
– [Lexy] I despise sports metaphors.

00:12:54.553 --> 00:12:58.800
– She probably dislikes sports metaphors because of&nbsp;
the “Super Bowl of slaughter” speech that Chucky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:03.240
gave Jake in Season 1, that almost convinced&nbsp;
him to take Lexy out. He’s an instant replay.

00:13:03.979 --> 00:13:07.159
– It's the Super Bowl of slaughter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:14.220
And you can't just sit in the stands, you know?&nbsp;
We all gotta get out there and get in the game.

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:18.712
Unfortunately for Lexy, there would be an all&nbsp;
out blitz of sports metaphors in Season 2.

00:13:18.712 --> 00:13:23.160
– [Bryce] I'm sure you boys are anxious to get on the&nbsp;
straight and narrow, get your lives back on track,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:26.164
back on the right track, back on the fast track.

00:13:26.164 --> 00:13:28.351
– I just love sports metaphors.

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:31.860
– Episode 3 would be titled “Hail Mary!”,&nbsp;
which in addition to religious practice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:35.040
is also a play in football, which&nbsp;
is usually used as a last ditch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.980
effort at the end of the game. Not&nbsp;
that I would know, as a Bears fan.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:42.120
It makes sense though, because brainwashing&nbsp;
Chucky is Jake’s last ditch attempt to give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:46.646
himself closure about what happened to Gary.&nbsp;
Unfortunately, he’s underestimated his opponent.

00:13:46.646 --> 00:13:50.100
– [Chucky] I should know. I’m&nbsp;
like the MVP of serial murder.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:54.240
– [Zac] He even manages to pull off the upset&nbsp;
in episode 5, against Buff Chucky.

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:56.220
– How did I do, coach?

00:13:56.220 --> 00:13:59.040
– And, later on, in preparation&nbsp;
to go up against The Colonel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:01.380
Jake works another sports&nbsp;
metaphor into his gameplan.

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:05.272
– You know, whatever battle this Colonel has&nbsp;
brewing, we need to have it on our own terms.&nbsp;

00:14:05.272 --> 00:14:07.800
– And what terms would those be?
– Home court advantage.

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:11.760
– All those sports metaphors have got me&nbsp;
gassed, so I’m gonna take a short timeout,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:15.480
but when I come back, I’m gonna be&nbsp;
dealing even more Things You Missed.

00:14:15.663 --> 00:14:17.663
(impact)

00:14:20.267 --> 00:14:22.267
(tense music)

00:14:24.601 --> 00:14:25.993
Outside of the threat of Chucky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.993 --> 00:14:30.300
there is another evil lurking in the halls&nbsp;
of Incarnate Lord, Lexy’s childhood bully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:34.440
Trevor. In season 1, Lexy was the bully, so&nbsp;
she tries to channel some of that energy to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:37.920
push back against Trevor -- effectively&nbsp;
creating a Bully vs Bully scenario.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:41.760
When I first saw this, I wondered if it&nbsp;
could be foreshadowing of an eventual Chucky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:46.260
vs Chucky battle of some kind, and it later&nbsp;
came to fruition. But in order to get there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:50.340
the 2nd Chucky had to be snuck into the&nbsp;
school, so a Good Guy doll is mailed as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:53.448
part of Sister Ruth’s Christmas toy drive&nbsp;
-- even though it’s still weeks away.

00:14:53.448 --> 00:14:57.060
– [Bryce] That’s wonderful sister&nbsp;
Elizabeth. No time like the present.

00:14:57.060 --> 00:15:02.580
– Is that… supposed to be a pun? Cause&nbsp;
present? Like… Christmas present?

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:06.120
The students aren’t supposed to have access&nbsp;
to phones, so the trio has theirs confiscated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:10.620
and noted on this document, to keep track of&nbsp;
which phone belongs to whom. Let’s zoom in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.620 --> 00:15:15.060
names. One of them is Mauro LaCaprara. This&nbsp;
is the name of a production designer who has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:20.040
worked on many major TV shows filmed in Toronto,&nbsp;
such as the Handmaid’s Tale and Clarice. Chucky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:24.300
was also filmed in Toronto. It doesn’t appear&nbsp;
that he worked on it, but many of his jobs went&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:28.500
uncredited, so that could be the case again. I’m&nbsp;
gonna count it as a crew reference easter egg.

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:30.360
And speaking of it being filmed in Toronto,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:34.620
Lexy has two posters in her room of the small&nbsp;
Toronto based rock back Kingdom of Birds.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:40.020
As Sister Elizabeth is tagging each of the gifts,&nbsp;
there are a few more crew references. This red tag is labeled:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:44.460
The Mancini Family after CHUCKY series&nbsp;
creator Don Mancini. The white tag says:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:49.020
The Colavecchia Family, named after David and John&nbsp;
Colavecchia, who worked in the camera department.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:54.420
The green tag says The Mrkobrada Family. James&nbsp;
and Steve Mrkobrada also worked camera department.

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:58.080
There’s also a tough to spot easter egg in&nbsp;
Episode 1, when Lexy is rummaging through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:01.980
her mother’s medicine cabinet, one of the&nbsp;
bottles was prescribed by Dr. Douglas Gabor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:05.940
which is a slightly altered version of Gabriella&nbsp;
Douglas, the first assistant art director

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:09.660
There’s not another crew reference easter&nbsp;
egg until episode 7, when Bryce brings out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:13.320
the Exorcism for Dummies book, which is a play&nbsp;
on the Voodoo for Dummies book introduced in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:17.940
Bride. Exorcism for Dummies is written by Richard&nbsp;
Darling, a reference to Rick Darling the property&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:22.140
master on both Seasons 1 and 2. It turns out&nbsp;
that Tiffany held onto Voodoo for Dummies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:27.060
we see it again in Episode 8. It’s written by&nbsp;
Don Mancini, our last crew reference easter egg.

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:30.420
While not technically a crew reference,&nbsp;
there is a meta-horror moment when Jake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:33.840
comments that Father Bryce reminds him&nbsp;
of his dad. That’s because Mr. Wheeler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:37.860
his brother Logan, and Father Bryce are&nbsp;
all played by the same actor: Devon Sawa.

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:42.060
The first victim this season… other&nbsp;
than Tiffany, and all those Chuckys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:46.140
and Gary… is Sister Elizabeth who&nbsp;
has a heart attack upon seeing him.

00:16:46.140 --> 00:16:49.987
– Just looking at me is scary&nbsp;
enough to give you a heart attack?

00:16:49.987 --> 00:16:53.640
– He shouldn’t be that surprised, because this has&nbsp;
happened before. It’s a reference to the way that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:58.080
Colonel Cochrane was killed in Child’s Play 3, and&nbsp;
it’s another reason I thought Season 2 was going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:02.160
to be a tribute to that third movie. But, as you&nbsp;
know, it went in the direction of Seed of Chucky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:06.660
carrying on its tradition of bombarding us with&nbsp;
needless pop-culture references. I’m gonna go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:09.720
through them, but if you’re not interested in&nbsp;
that, feel free to skip to the next chapter.

00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:11.520
When Chucky holds them hostage at the beginning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:11.520 --> 00:17:15.600
he mocks their friendship for not spending&nbsp;
time together, and this is Devon’s rebuttal.

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:19.320
– We’ve been busy.
– Well now you’re all gonna get busy dying.

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:22.100
– That might be a reference&nbsp;
to The Shawshank Redemption.

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:30.840
– I guess it comes down to a simple&nbsp;
choice really. Get busy living. Or get busy dying.

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:32.820
– I’m sure you didn’t miss the Scooby Doo reference.

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:36.660
– …and I wouldn’t have gotten away with it&nbsp;
too if it weren’t for you meddling kids.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:41.680
– After the truck crash, the head of the female&nbsp;
doll somehow ends up in Tiffany’s bed. (screams)

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:45.660
A parody of the horse head scene&nbsp;
from The Godfather. (screams)

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:50.629
Later that day, Tiffany can be seen watching&nbsp;
Liar, Liar, when Nica makes this comment.

00:17:50.629 --> 00:17:54.780
– [Nica] I know you went through all&nbsp;
of Jennifer Tilly’s Simpsons money.

00:17:54.780 --> 00:17:59.400
– Jennifer Tilly isn’t on the Simpsons, so what’s&nbsp;
the deal with this? Luckily, I happen to know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:03.480
a Simpson’s expert who can explain it much&nbsp;
better than I can. Here’s The Simpson’s Theory.

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:09.900
– Hey guys! Now I want to start off by saying that although Jennifer&nbsp;
Tilly wasn't a regular cast member of The Simpsons, she was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:16.980
previously married to late Simpsons co-creator&nbsp;
Sam Simon, and when it came to their divorce in 1993, a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:21.120
percentage of Simon's payments from Fox was awarded to her.

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:25.500
Then she later appeared as herself&nbsp;
on Season 24’s “Gone Abie Gone”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:28.740
where she even references said Simpsons Money.

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:32.730
– I've read every expert on poker,&nbsp;
and watched Jennifer Tilly's DVD.&nbsp;

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:36.240
– Start with your Simpsons&nbsp;
Money. Use the little girl voice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:42.267
and take them for everything they've got. Now,&nbsp;
I'm needed on the set of Bride of Chucky V.

00:18:42.401 --> 00:18:46.271
– And there you have it folks. That is your random Simpsons fact of the day. 

00:18:46.271 --> 00:18:48.120
Thans so much for having me on, Zac.

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:51.420
– Thank you Lydia. I’ll put a link to her&nbsp;
channel in the description. Moving along,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:55.320
when the kids try to reprogram Chucky, they&nbsp;
clip his eyes open using what appears to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:59.340
hairclips as a parody of the brainwashing scene&nbsp;
in A Clockwork Orange, where Alex is conditioned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:03.420
to feel nausea whenever he’s exposed to violence,&nbsp;
which is exactly what happens to Chucky. Instead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:07.320
of showing him war footage, they show him&nbsp;
horror movies, like The Thing and Psycho II.

00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:11.520
In Episode 4, the twins invite some guests over&nbsp;
to celebrate their birthday behind Tiffany’s back.

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:15.780
– We figured you wouldn’t want to have people&nbsp;
over given your Norma Desmond vibes as of late.

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:20.220
– [Zac] Norma Desmond is the forgotten silent movie&nbsp;
star in the 1950 noir film Sunset Blvd,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:23.820
who, similar to Tiffany, never leaves&nbsp;
her mansion and revels in the past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:27.420
watching her own old movies. In Tiffany’s&nbsp;
case, they aren’t actually her movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:30.780
but you get the point. Both characters&nbsp;
are delusional -- and insane.

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:34.860
Not long after, Tiffany apologizes to her&nbsp;
guests for being a recluse over the last year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:39.000
and says she’s entering her Garbo era. This&nbsp;
is a reference to another silent film star,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:43.500
Greta Garbo, who is known for her melancholic&nbsp;
roles. So, essentially nothing like Tiffany&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:46.980
or Jennifer Tilly, which makes it kind&nbsp;
of funny if you know who Greta Garbo is.

00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:49.860
Later on, when Buff Chucky&nbsp;
is discovered by Sister Ruth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:49.860 --> 00:19:52.800
who mistakes him for a God, he&nbsp;
makes more of a 90s reference.

00:19:54.093 --> 00:19:56.304
– [Chucky] I like your style, Sister Act.

00:19:56.304 --> 00:19:57.634
– Sister Ruth.

00:19:57.863 --> 00:20:01.500
– Sister Act is a comedy franchise starring&nbsp;
Whoopie Goldberg. Nevermind the fact Chucky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:06.300
was dead in 1992 when the first one came out,&nbsp;
dead in 1993 when the second one came out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:11.040
and was literally just a dismembered arm in&nbsp;
2006 when the broadway musical premiered. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:13.860
creators of this show clearly care&nbsp;
a lot more about referencing their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:17.100
favorite IPs than having their&nbsp;
own show make any logical sense.

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:22.140
It gets really bad shortly after. When I first saw&nbsp;
the bald Chucky known as The Colonel, I thought it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:22.140 --> 00:20:25.860
had something to do with the end of Child’s&nbsp;
Play 2 or beginning of Child’s Play 3, where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:25.860 --> 00:20:29.640
we see the factory that the Good Guys are made&nbsp;
in, and some of them have not received hair yet.

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:33.840
It wasn’t until this very strange scene&nbsp;
that I ended up looking into the character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:38.220
and discovered who he’s really supposed&nbsp;
to be… and I have a lot to say about it.

00:20:38.691 --> 00:20:40.691
(impact)

00:20:43.171 --> 00:20:47.662
(war march music)

00:20:47.662 --> 00:20:52.020
The Colonel Chucky is a reference to an&nbsp;
iconic character from a 1979 war movie known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:56.520
as Apocalypse Now. His name is Colonel Walter&nbsp;
Kurtz, and he is a rogue army officer who went&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:56.520 --> 00:21:00.240
insane and started commanding his own troops&nbsp;
in Cambodia, kind of like how The Colonel in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:04.140
Chucky sets up his own camp in the wilderness and&nbsp;
commands his own unit of Good Guy dolls.

00:21:04.140 --> 00:21:07.560
After Andy gets the better of him in&nbsp;
Episode 6, The Colonel repeatedly says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:07.560 --> 00:21:11.640
“the horror” before passing away, a clear&nbsp;
takeoff of Colonel Kurtz’s final moments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:16.500
in Apocalypse Now. We’re shown Flashbacks of&nbsp;
the Vietnam war. Charles Lee Ray was never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:20.820
in the Vietnam war -- it began before&nbsp;
he was born and ended when he was 16.

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:25.260
In my opinion, the mere act of referencing another&nbsp;
property doesn’t make it funny. If you’re doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:29.880
it in a way that adds entertainment value, that’s&nbsp;
one thing, but just putting a random war flashback&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:34.020
that doesn’t even fit, just because Francis Ford&nbsp;
Coppola did it, isn’t all that entertaining.

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:38.400
Let’s look at The Simpsons again as an example.&nbsp;
The Simpsons love a good parody episode. Every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:42.240
year they do Treehouse of Horror. But part of the&nbsp;
fun of watching Treehouse of Horror is learning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:42.240 --> 00:21:45.960
how the established characters of Springfield&nbsp;
will change a horror story that we already know.

00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:48.660
In the Treehouse of Horror III,&nbsp;
segment “Clown Without Pity”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:52.560
Homer buys his son a talking Krusty doll for&nbsp;
his birthday. It’s a parody of Child’s Play,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:55.920
but they don’t just run through the plot of&nbsp;
the movie, they use the talking murder doll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:55.920 --> 00:21:59.460
concept in a way that fits the style&nbsp;
and humor we love in the Simpsons.

00:21:59.899 --> 00:22:04.080
– Take this object, but beware,&nbsp;
it carries a terrible curse.&nbsp;

00:22:04.080 --> 00:22:07.440
– Ooh, that’s bad.
– But it comes with a free frogurt!&nbsp;

00:22:07.440 --> 00:22:10.980
– That’s good!
– The frogurt is also cursed.&nbsp;

00:22:10.980 --> 00:22:13.860
– That’s bad.
– But you get your choice of topping.&nbsp;

00:22:13.860 --> 00:22:17.700
– That’s good!
– The toppings contain potassium benzoate…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:19.500 --> 00:22:21.480
that’s bad.
– Can I go now?

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:25.200
– You don’t have to have seen Child’s Play&nbsp;
to appreciate “Clown Without Pity”. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:25.200 --> 00:22:28.620
if you haven’t seen Apocalypse Now,&nbsp;
good luck understanding what the hell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:32.580
that Colonel Kurtz reference was. Also&nbsp;
his scene is a total disaster. Roll it.

00:22:33.596 --> 00:22:36.859
– Give me liberty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:36.859 --> 00:22:42.919
or give me death… Remember the Alamo!

00:22:43.169 --> 00:22:45.169
Auuughhhh!

00:22:47.559 --> 00:22:48.599
– [Lexy] Who's Khan?

00:22:48.599 --> 00:22:53.377
– What is going on here? Why is Lexy asking “who’s&nbsp;
Khan?” It almost feels like she’s responding to a

00:22:53.400 --> 00:22:57.660
line that was cut from the show. Has the editing&nbsp;
really gotten that bad? Here’s my last thing on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:57.660 --> 00:23:01.800
this topic. When your media references are just&nbsp;
references for the sake of references, you start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:01.800 --> 00:23:07.080
to lose clarity of if they ever are references.&nbsp;
For example, take Tiffany’s line towards Caroline…

00:23:07.080 --> 00:23:08.700
– [Tiffany] Clever girl!

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:11.220
– Like, was that supposed to&nbsp;
be a Jurassic Park reference?

00:23:11.220 --> 00:23:13.494
– Clever girl!

00:23:13.494 --> 00:23:17.940
– Or was she just calling Caroline clever? You&nbsp;
can’t even tell anymore. Anyway, rant over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:17.940 --> 00:23:20.880
let’s get back to where we were.&nbsp;
Episode 2. I mentioned that Tiffany&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:20.880 --> 00:23:24.300
was watching Jennifer Tilly’s performance&nbsp;
in Liar, Liar, and in that same episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:24.300 --> 00:23:27.900
Father Bryce makes Jake read&nbsp;
a biblical passage about lies.

00:23:27.900 --> 00:23:34.320
– [Jake] When he lies, he speaks according to his own&nbsp;
nature, for he is a liar, and the father of lies.

00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:37.020
– It’s very fitting that lies are&nbsp;
such a big focus on this episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:40.500
because Chucky’s lies would have a major&nbsp;
impact. When he acts as if he’s been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:40.500 --> 00:23:43.740
changed by the Clockwork Orange treatment,&nbsp;
the characters drop their guard around him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:43.740 --> 00:23:46.380
allowing him to make one of the most&nbsp;
devastating kills of the series.

00:23:46.380 --> 00:23:51.180
Moving on to Episode 3, we meet Father O’Malley,&nbsp;
who is clearly tired of Nadine coming in every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:51.180 --> 00:23:55.380
week to do confession with him. The character is a&nbsp;
tribute to Reverend William O’Malley, who is known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:55.380 --> 00:24:00.060
for his portrayal of Father Dyer in The Exorcist,&nbsp;
where he also served as a technical advisor. Of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:00.060 --> 00:24:04.200
all the films that Chucky Season 2 imitates,&nbsp;
the strongest influence, other than Scream, is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:04.200 --> 00:24:08.100
probably The Exorcist, but I’ll come back to that&nbsp;
later in this video when I talk about the ending.

00:24:08.100 --> 00:24:11.280
During stage 1 of the brainwashing&nbsp;
scene, one of the disturbing clips&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:11.280 --> 00:24:14.820
they show Chucky is someone falling out&nbsp;
of a window onto a car -- it’s the exact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:14.820 --> 00:24:18.600
same as the first kill we ever saw Chucky&nbsp;
make, Aunt Maggie in the original movie.

00:24:18.600 --> 00:24:20.149
(slam)

00:24:20.149 --> 00:24:24.163
Then during stage 2, he sees Nadine&nbsp;
setting up the phone and says this.

00:24:24.163 --> 00:24:30.960
– Aunt Maggie. Chucky wants&nbsp;
to watch the 9 o’clock news.

00:24:31.560 --> 00:24:35.160
– This is the exact like said by Andy in&nbsp;
the, shortly after meeting Chucky in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:35.160 --> 00:24:39.660
original. In his dazed state, this was probably&nbsp;
triggered by seeing Nadine, who looks similar to,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:39.660 --> 00:24:43.140
and has the same hairstyle as Aunt&nbsp;
Maggie. It’s also foreshadowing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:43.140 --> 00:24:47.100
because he eventually kills Nadine the 
same way he killed Aunt Maggie: by throwing her out a window.

00:24:47.100 --> 00:24:50.760
She ends up landing on a statue of the&nbsp;
virgin Mary, causing the image to resemble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:50.760 --> 00:24:55.380
Michelangelo’s sculpture, Pietà, which depicts&nbsp;
Jesus dying in the arms of Mary. I feel like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:55.380 --> 00:24:59.220
this may be connected to Nadine returning as an&nbsp;
angel, but I don’t really know anything about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:59.220 --> 00:25:03.120
the Catholic lore. There’s also a shot while&nbsp;
Nadine is doing her “Hail Marys” where she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:03.120 --> 00:25:07.560
pats a smaller statue on the head, maybe a small&nbsp;
clue that she’ll be landing on a statue’s head.

00:25:07.560 --> 00:25:11.040
After the brainwashing is complete Lexy&nbsp;
is tasked with keeping an eye on Chucky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:11.040 --> 00:25:14.700
and he asks her a variety of annoying&nbsp;
questions, one of which is “do you have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:14.700 --> 00:25:19.471
a cat”? This is a callback to season 1 episode 1
where Chucky’s first victim is Jake's cat.

00:25:19.471 --> 00:25:22.467
We also see him take out a cat in the 2019 remake.

00:25:22.467 --> 00:25:27.715
Episode 4 is a weird one -- it’s called Death&nbsp;
on Denial, a play on Death on the Nile, a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:27.715 --> 00:25:32.280
1978 murder mystery film, which is fitting because&nbsp;
this episode is all about a murder mystery party.

00:25:32.280 --> 00:25:33.720
There’s a line that caught my attention,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:33.720 --> 00:25:38.520
where Glenda mentions having spoken to Tiffany&nbsp;
/ Jennifer’s accountant, Stan. Stan was the name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:38.520 --> 00:25:42.900
of Jennifer’s limo driver / secret lover in Seed.
He appeared to have died at the end of that movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:42.900 --> 00:25:47.640
but then again, so did Jennifer Tilly. However,&nbsp;
when we meet Jennifer Tilly, she appears to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:47.640 --> 00:25:51.720
be Tiffany’s accountant? I’m not really sure&nbsp;
what’s going on here, or if we’ll ever find out.

00:25:51.720 --> 00:25:55.140
Before the guests arrive, the three can be&nbsp;
seen eating Swedish Meatballs for dinner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:55.140 --> 00:25:57.960
Tiffany’s specialty, and&nbsp;
Chucky’s supposed favorite food.

00:25:57.960 --> 00:26:00.900
Speaking of favorite foods, when the&nbsp;
real Jennifer Tilly finally does appear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:00.900 --> 00:26:03.420
she’s got one thing on her mind. Roll it.

00:26:04.413 --> 00:26:07.620
–  I’m starving. You promised me chocolate.

00:26:07.620 --> 00:26:10.200
– Funny enough, chocolate is&nbsp;
what got her into this mess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:10.200 --> 00:26:13.620
in the first place. She only encountered&nbsp;
Tiffany Valentine because she snuck into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:13.620 --> 00:26:16.440
a prop room at the movie studio&nbsp;
to secretly snack on chocolate.

00:26:16.440 --> 00:26:19.920
If you’re like me, you probably had a&nbsp;
lot of questions about this party that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:19.920 --> 00:26:24.600
remain unanswered. Primarily, why is Glen and&nbsp;
Glenda’s birthday being celebrated in November,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:24.600 --> 00:26:28.080
when we already know that they were&nbsp;
born in March 2004? I swear they’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:28.080 --> 00:26:30.420
just trying to make the timeline&nbsp;
difficult for me at this point…

00:26:30.420 --> 00:26:35.100
But who are these seemingly random party&nbsp;
guests? What is their significance? And why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:35.100 --> 00:26:39.660
does this butler look so familiar? I have&nbsp;
all the answers that Liv Morgan didn’t.

00:26:39.961 --> 00:26:41.961
(impact)

00:26:45.097 --> 00:26:48.606
(girly pop music)

00:26:48.606 --> 00:26:52.260
The twins wanted a surprise party, so&nbsp;
they invited some of their mother’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:52.260 --> 00:26:56.340
friends to the house without her knowing&nbsp;
to “surprise” them. This already doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:56.340 --> 00:26:58.920
make sense, but it may have been&nbsp;
a strategy to help distract her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:58.920 --> 00:27:02.880
making it easier for Glen and Glenda&nbsp;
to sneak out Nica. So who are these people?

00:27:02.880 --> 00:27:07.200
Auntie Gina is introduced first. She isn’t&nbsp;
anyone’s real aunt, I think she’s more of an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:07.200 --> 00:27:10.740
honorary aunt for the twins, kind of like&nbsp;
how Aunt Maggie wasn’t Andy’s real Aunt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:10.740 --> 00:27:14.520
she was just a friend of his mother. Her full&nbsp;
name is Gina Gershon, and she co-starred with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:14.520 --> 00:27:18.660
Jennifer Tilly in the 1996 thriller, Bound,&nbsp;
where the two shared a lesbian relationship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:18.660 --> 00:27:22.440
which we find out is real in the world&nbsp;
of CHUCKY. In fact, when Gina sneaks up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:22.440 --> 00:27:25.980
on her in the bedroom, you can see the Bound&nbsp;
poster in the background at that very moment.

00:27:25.980 --> 00:27:31.800
Similarly, Uncle Pants is not Glen and Glenda’s&nbsp;
real uncle, he’s Joe Pantaliano, another actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:31.800 --> 00:27:35.700
friend, who was also in Bound, where he plays&nbsp;
Jennifer Tilly’s boyfriend, Caesar. Apparently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:35.700 --> 00:27:40.020
he too has an ongoing relationship with her, we&nbsp;
literally see him caught with his pants down.

00:27:40.020 --> 00:27:44.400
Then there’s Sutton Stracke. I guess Jennifer&nbsp;
and Sutton are just friends in real life. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:44.400 --> 00:27:48.780
final guest is Meg Tilly, the real life sister of&nbsp;
Jennifer Tilly. When I first heard that she was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:48.780 --> 00:27:52.920
going to be cast for Season 2, I assumed she would&nbsp;
be playing Tiffany’s sister, who was referenced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:52.920 --> 00:27:58.740
in Seed, and as far as we know, still alive. But I&nbsp;
was wrong, she’s just playing herself. Ironically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:58.740 --> 00:28:03.720
Meg actually is Glen and Glenda’s aunt, because&nbsp;
the twins’ biological mother is Jennifer Tilly.

00:28:03.720 --> 00:28:07.380
The Butler is the only who isn’t playing&nbsp;
himself, but if he still looks familiar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:07.380 --> 00:28:11.640
it may be because the actor, Tony Nappo,&nbsp;
played Gus Colyard in the Saw franchise.

00:28:11.640 --> 00:28:17.460
As if that wasn’t enough star power, the episode&nbsp;
ends with a sit-down between Chucky and WWE star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:17.460 --> 00:28:22.500
Liv Morgan, and I just gotta say: what is the&nbsp;
deal lately with these WWE stars being able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:22.500 --> 00:28:27.600
manipulate entertainers for guest spots, seemingly&nbsp;
at will? Between this, the “Alexa Bliss” song by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:27.600 --> 00:28:32.520
Bowling for Soup, and the time Dead Meat did&nbsp;
like a whole podcast season of just WWE stars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:32.520 --> 00:28:37.080
I’d like to know who runs their marketing team.&nbsp;
Or maybe you just have to be a WWE fan to get it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:37.080 --> 00:28:41.820
But I guess if Justin Fields randomly wanted&nbsp;
to come on CZsWorld, yeah, I’d probably do it.

00:28:41.820 --> 00:28:45.780
There's one more item I’d like to point out in this&nbsp;
episode, but I do need to spoil the movie Psycho&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:45.780 --> 00:28:50.298
to do it, so spoiler alert until the end of this&nbsp;
chapter. After the butler is found, and everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:50.298 --> 00:28:54.570
is discussing who the killer could be, the finger&nbsp;
is pointed at Glen and Glenda, to which Glen says:

00:28:54.570 --> 00:28:56.040
– We wouldn’t hurt a fly.

00:28:56.040 --> 00:28:59.880
– Those who have seen my Seed of Chucky episode&nbsp;
may have picked up on this. In that movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:59.880 --> 00:29:03.600
Glen and Glenda are a split personality&nbsp;
both trapped inside the body of this doll,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:03.600 --> 00:29:07.680
switching back and forth in regards to who is&nbsp;
in control. It’s the same concept as Norman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:07.680 --> 00:29:11.760
and Norma Bates in Psycho, and as a result,&nbsp;
there are a ton of Psycho references in Seed.

00:29:11.760 --> 00:29:14.880
So this line is also a Psycho&nbsp;
reference. At the end of the movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:14.880 --> 00:29:19.237
we hear Norma’s internal monologue,&nbsp;
and in an attempt to look innocent, she says this. 

00:29:19.237 --> 00:29:23.880
– They’re probably watching me. Let them&nbsp;
see what kind of a person I am… I’m not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:23.880 --> 00:29:30.420
even gonna swat that fly. …and they’ll&nbsp;
say ‘why she wouldn’t even harm a fly’.

00:29:30.420 --> 00:29:35.340
– And this idea comes back a couple episodes&nbsp;
later, as Jake, Devon, Lexy and Nadine are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:35.340 --> 00:29:39.240
still trying to determine if their reprogrammed&nbsp;
Chucky is really dangerous or not. He literally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:39.240 --> 00:29:42.780
kills a fly, foreshadowing that he’s not&nbsp;
the harmless doll that Jake thinks he is.

00:29:42.780 --> 00:29:46.620
One more (maybe?) Psycho reference,&nbsp;
when Tiffany slices up Meg Tilly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:46.620 --> 00:29:48.780
the music sounds a lot like the music in Psycho.

00:29:48.991 --> 00:29:50.991
(dramatic music)

00:29:52.080 --> 00:29:55.320
After awakening from a bad dream,&nbsp;
Glen can be seen reading Great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:55.320 --> 00:29:58.440
Expectations. This novel was written&nbsp;
by British author Charles Dickens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:58.440 --> 00:30:02.940
a callback to Glen’s childhood spent in the UK&nbsp;
before ever being reborn as a human. That day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:02.940 --> 00:30:07.140
when Tiffany asks what happened to Nica and&nbsp;
Glenda, I noticed Glen’s eye give a little twitch.

00:30:07.140 --> 00:30:09.453
– Tell me where Glenda took Nica.

00:30:11.438 --> 00:30:14.760
– This is something that happened in Seed,&nbsp;
Glen’s eye would twitch under stressful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:14.760 --> 00:30:16.860
circumstances that are just too much to deal with.

00:30:16.860 --> 00:30:19.920
Tiffany’s outfit during this scene&nbsp;
contains these strange playing cards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:19.920 --> 00:30:22.320
probably referencing her career&nbsp;
as a professional poker player,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:22.320 --> 00:30:26.580
which I talked about in Season 1. Anyway,&nbsp;
after Glen discovers the real Jen Tilly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:26.580 --> 00:30:31.020
trapped in doll form, Tiffany BURNS DOWN&nbsp;
THE HOUSE which feels very unnecessary.

00:30:31.020 --> 00:30:34.680
Back at the school, the brainwashed scout&nbsp;
Chucky fights and defeats Buff Chucky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:34.680 --> 00:30:37.560
and in the aftermath Father Bryce&nbsp;
orders Sister Ruth to throw away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:37.560 --> 00:30:40.440
the tattered doll. It’s an important&nbsp;
Chucky tradition for someone to try&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:40.440 --> 00:30:43.860
to trash the antagonistic toy -- this is&nbsp;
the eighth time someone has attempted it.

00:30:43.860 --> 00:30:46.860
As we get further into the season&nbsp;
there are more and more callbacks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:46.860 --> 00:30:48.720
to the original movie series. For example:

00:30:48.720 --> 00:30:53.340
Andy is now being kept prisoner by Chucky, in&nbsp;
a cabin, where he’s tortured. It’s revenge for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:53.340 --> 00:30:57.600
when Andy kept Chucky’s head as his prisoner,&nbsp;
in his cabin, and tortured him. Cool detail&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:57.600 --> 00:31:00.900
about the cabin, if you bring up the lights,&nbsp;
you can see many knives stored overhead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:00.900 --> 00:31:03.900
probably the knives of each of the&nbsp;
Chucky’s that The Colonel has killed.

00:31:03.900 --> 00:31:07.980
Sister Ruth is the next to discover that&nbsp;
Chucky is alive, and he tells her that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:07.980 --> 00:31:11.340
should be blonde. He told Tiffany the&nbsp;
same thing when they first met in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:11.340 --> 00:31:15.180
flashback during Season 1, which suggests&nbsp;
that Chucky has a thing for Sister Ruth.

00:31:15.180 --> 00:31:18.780
As Kyle, Nica, and Glenda are staying&nbsp;
in a hotel en route to New Jersey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:18.780 --> 00:31:22.860
Kyle has a pack of cigarettes labeled&nbsp;
“Kincaid”. As far as I know, this isn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:22.860 --> 00:31:27.120
a brand you can still find, so it must be a&nbsp;
reference to Jade Kincaid from Bride of Chucky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:27.120 --> 00:31:31.440
one of the few surviving characters who has yet&nbsp;
to make an appearance in the TV series. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:31.440 --> 00:31:35.640
Kyle has a necklace that says “Mom” on it,&nbsp;
which is a strange thing for an orphan to have.

00:31:35.640 --> 00:31:39.720
A report comes on the TV, breaking the news&nbsp;
that Jennifer Tilly is now wanted for murder.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:39.720 --> 00:31:43.920
The photo that they use is from the 2019&nbsp;
Saturn Awards. The Saturns were briefly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:43.920 --> 00:31:48.000
mentioned by Jake and Devon in Season 1. If you’re&nbsp;
curious, the photo used in the 2nd news report,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:48.000 --> 00:31:50.640
where Tiffany freaks out about the&nbsp;
terrible picture they used of her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:50.640 --> 00:31:55.140
was taken at the premiere of Panic Room in 2002.&nbsp;
It’s weird that they would use such an old photo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:55.140 --> 00:31:59.520
but it’s a perfect opportunity for me to promote&nbsp;
my Things You Missed episode on Panic Room.

00:31:59.520 --> 00:32:04.080
At Lord Incarnate, Father Bryce puts the school&nbsp;
on lockdown, but Lexy and Nadine are able to reach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:04.080 --> 00:32:07.800
Jake and Devon’s room anyways, by climbing&nbsp;
out their window and into the boys’ window.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:07.800 --> 00:32:12.300
They probably expected us to forget that they&nbsp;
showed the outside of Lexy and Nadine’s room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:12.300 --> 00:32:16.680
and unless they are both Spider-man, they’re&nbsp;
no way the girls pulled this off. The creators&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:16.680 --> 00:32:20.280
of this show need to stop underestimating me.&nbsp;
I didn’t forget when the twins' birthday is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:20.280 --> 00:32:22.860
and I didn’t forget what the exterior&nbsp;
of the school looks like either.

00:32:22.860 --> 00:32:27.180
Andy helps them ambush and defeat The Colonel,&nbsp;
but before he can get to the scout, Dr. Mixter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:27.180 --> 00:32:31.500
shows up with a gun and takes Chucky away. I’m&nbsp;
not quite sure how they let her do this. Yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:31.500 --> 00:32:34.920
she has a gun, but there are 5 of&nbsp;
them, if she even tried to use the gun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:34.920 --> 00:32:38.220
the rest of them could quickly pounce&nbsp;
on her. Then, she somehow beats up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:38.220 --> 00:32:41.820
Andy? She has a chance to shoot him right&nbsp;
here, but she doesn't, for some reason.

00:32:41.820 --> 00:32:46.020
Episode 7 is called "Goin' to the Chapel". I&nbsp;
think it's referring to a lyric from the Dixie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:46.020 --> 00:32:50.160
Cups song, "Chapel of Love". This episode is&nbsp;
all about the exorcism of Scout Chucky to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:50.160 --> 00:32:54.120
room for Chucky Prime to leave Nica's body.&nbsp;
We later find out this is kinda pointless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:54.120 --> 00:32:57.840
because Dr. Mixter already has a backup&nbsp;
Chucky in her safe… I'll ignore that though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:57.840 --> 00:33:00.360
because I have something else&nbsp;
I'd like to complain about.

00:33:00.604 --> 00:33:02.604
(impact)

00:33:05.903 --> 00:33:09.751
(suspenseful music)

00:33:09.751 --> 00:33:13.560
The biggest obstacle that the characters have&nbsp;
to overcome in every installment is Chucky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:13.560 --> 00:33:18.480
but there are also obstacles on a character level&nbsp;
in each movie. In Child’s Play, Andy is not taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:18.480 --> 00:33:22.500
seriously because he’s a kid. In Curse, Nica&nbsp;
wants to get her family to see her as a person,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:22.500 --> 00:33:26.880
not see her for her disability. Season 2&nbsp;
is all about Jake and Devon wanting those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:26.880 --> 00:33:30.540
around them to accept their relationship.&nbsp;
They are trapped in a school and religion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:30.540 --> 00:33:34.740
that doesn’t accept them. They’re constantly&nbsp;
trying to invalidate that religion. So I just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:34.740 --> 00:33:38.880
find it weird that they successfully perform&nbsp;
an exorcism at the end, because doesn’t that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:38.880 --> 00:33:43.080
kind of say that the religion really does have&nbsp;
power? It’s not super shocking, because Voodoo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:43.080 --> 00:33:47.640
is a religion that gave Chucky power in the very&nbsp;
first movie, but it feels somewhat contradictory.

00:33:47.640 --> 00:33:51.000
The deal to perform the exorcism is&nbsp;
struck when Kyle shows up with a gun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:51.000 --> 00:33:52.980
leveling the playing field against Dr. Mixter.

00:33:52.980 --> 00:33:54.600
– What did you do to your hair?

00:33:54.921 --> 00:33:56.280
– I wasn't having any fun as a blonde.

00:33:56.280 --> 00:33:58.860
– Because holding each other at gun&nbsp;
pointpoint is the perfect time to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:58.860 --> 00:34:01.200
strike up casual conversations about women’s hair.

00:34:01.200 --> 00:34:04.260
At this point, everyone is brought&nbsp;
together to help perform the exorcism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:04.260 --> 00:34:07.560
other than Tiffany, Jennifer and Glen,&nbsp;
who are still on their way. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:07.560 --> 00:34:11.580
Jennifer would not make it. After 18&nbsp;
years of being trapped inside this doll,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:11.580 --> 00:34:15.240
she seizes her opportunity to make a&nbsp;
run for it, and gets whacked by a truck.

00:34:15.240 --> 00:34:19.680
This is a franchise callback. David, from&nbsp;
Bride of Chucky, suffers the exact same fate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:19.680 --> 00:34:22.620
he’s hit by a truck while trying&nbsp;
to escape from Tiffany Valentine.

00:34:22.620 --> 00:34:26.760
While preparations are made to perform the&nbsp;
exorcism, Chucky is tied up, leaving him to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:26.760 --> 00:34:31.080
verbally torture everyone, so Andy locks Chucky&nbsp;
into a bookshelf. This is a reference to the way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:31.080 --> 00:34:35.612
that Hannibal Lector was tied up in Silence of&nbsp;
the Lambs, and he even pulls out the same line.

00:34:35.612 --> 00:34:36.995
– Closer!

00:34:37.688 --> 00:34:39.494
– Closer!

00:34:39.540 --> 00:34:44.220
– If you watched my Season 1 episode, you learned&nbsp;
about how Don Mancini’s time on the Hannibal TV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:44.220 --> 00:34:48.120
show may have been the reason that Chucky made the movie&nbsp;
to syndicated programming in the first place.

00:34:48.120 --> 00:34:51.960
But the episode is primarily more of a&nbsp;
takeoff on another classic horror film.

00:34:51.960 --> 00:34:56.970
– Your mother sucks ****s in hell.
– Yeah, we’ve all seen that movie too ***hole.

00:34:56.970 --> 00:35:01.080
– The movie he is referring to is The Exorcist,&nbsp;
where the little girl Regan is possessed by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:01.080 --> 00:35:05.460
demon Pazuzu to say the same line. Her possession&nbsp;
causes her to switch from the innocent girl to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:05.460 --> 00:35:09.540
the evil demon, hurling psychological attacks&nbsp;
at those tending to her. We see Scout Chucky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:09.540 --> 00:35:13.380
do the same thing, as he toggles between&nbsp;
“Good Chucky” and “Evil Chucky”. Chucky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:13.380 --> 00:35:18.120
also takes after Regan by projectile vomiting&nbsp;
a green substance and levitating up in the air,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:18.120 --> 00:35:22.440
just like in The Exorcist. The ending of The&nbsp;
Exorcist involves the possession being passed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:22.440 --> 00:35:27.120
the priest, shortly before his death, and Chucky&nbsp;
follows suit with the implosion of Father Bryce.

00:35:27.120 --> 00:35:29.460
Now all they have to do is transfer Chucky Prime’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:29.460 --> 00:35:32.880
soul out of Nica’s body into the doll.&nbsp;
However, all the guns have been locked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:32.880 --> 00:35:36.480
up at this point. I don’t understand why&nbsp;
they don’t just tie up Dr. Mixter first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:36.480 --> 00:35:41.700
then exorcize Chucky from Nica’s body -- but they&nbsp;
don’t think of that. THIS SHOW IS SO FRUSTRATING.

00:35:41.700 --> 00:35:45.420
This mistake allows Sister Ruth to show up&nbsp;
and rescue the newly transferred Chucky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:45.420 --> 00:35:49.320
but she’s stopped by Glenda, a knife&nbsp;
hidden away by Charles Lee Ray as kid.

00:35:49.320 --> 00:35:55.740
– I need you to go get my old Bowie knife, I&nbsp;
stashed it in a loose stone behind the church&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:55.740 --> 00:35:58.500
organ back in the day.
– No! No! Enough!

00:35:58.500 --> 00:36:02.040
– The season finale is called Chucky Actually,&nbsp;
because it takes place on Christmas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:02.040 --> 00:36:07.320
like the 2003 Christmas movie, Love Actually. We&nbsp;
see Dr. Mixter (now possessed by Chucky Prime),&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:07.320 --> 00:36:12.840
goes into the safe at her office to retrieve the&nbsp;
spare Good Guy doll. The safe passcode is 110988,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:12.840 --> 00:36:17.400
or 11/09/88, the release date of the&nbsp;
original Child’s Play. Another easter egg&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:17.400 --> 00:36:21.540
to the original is the maker of the safe:&nbsp;
Caputo Safe Co. This isn’t a real brand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:21.540 --> 00:36:25.080
so it must be another reference to&nbsp;
Charles’ old accomplice Eddie Caputo.

00:36:25.080 --> 00:36:28.380
The intro to this episode shows many of the&nbsp;
weapons that Chucky has used over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:28.380 --> 00:36:31.560
including the snake adorned knife&nbsp;
seen in the original and in Curse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:31.560 --> 00:36:33.900
the hammer used to knock Aunt Maggie&nbsp;
out the window in the original,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:33.900 --> 00:36:37.680
the red chainsaw that he would use later in&nbsp;
this episode, the generic kitchen knife which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:37.680 --> 00:36:41.880
has been used many times and the yardstick he&nbsp;
beat Ms. Kettlewell with in Child’s Play 2.

00:36:41.880 --> 00:36:44.640
Lexy asks her mom if her orphaned&nbsp;
friends can stay for the holidays&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:44.640 --> 00:36:48.420
while Mrs. Cross is live streaming.&nbsp;
She claims she was streaming to 100K&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:48.420 --> 00:36:51.840
followers. Which is total BS. If I&nbsp;
go on Twitch or YouTube right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:51.840 --> 00:36:56.760
the top channels are maybe getting a quarter of&nbsp;
that. I guarantee no one is tuning in to watch a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:56.760 --> 00:37:01.373
small town mayor decorate her Christmas tree. On&nbsp;
Facebook, no less. And later, she claims this:

00:37:01.373 --> 00:37:06.480
– My followers really seem to love my&nbsp;
nativity scene. It got over 30,000 likes.

00:37:06.480 --> 00:37:12.000
– No. There are only 45K people in Hackensack. Come&nbsp;
on. And when she’s streaming that nativity scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:12.000 --> 00:37:16.740
the onscreen phone POV doesn’t match how she’s&nbsp;
moving around the phone. How do you screw that up?

00:37:16.740 --> 00:37:20.100
Inside, Caroline and Belle (who&nbsp;
is secretly Chucky in disguise)&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:20.100 --> 00:37:23.580
are watching the news about what happened&nbsp;
at the Lord Incarnate school. This calls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:23.580 --> 00:37:27.540
back to Child’s Play 1, where Andy and Chucky&nbsp;
watch the news for updates on Eddie Caputo.

00:37:27.540 --> 00:37:30.420
I already talked about the defibrillator&nbsp;
used to take out the hospital security&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:30.420 --> 00:37:34.320
guy being another potential Child’s Play&nbsp;
reference. Like the shock device in 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:34.320 --> 00:37:38.880
why would they even have a tool powerful enough to&nbsp;
light someone on fire in the hospital? And are we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:38.880 --> 00:37:42.720
just supposed to assume that there are no smoke&nbsp;
detectors in this hospital? Make it make sense.

00:37:42.720 --> 00:37:47.880
The season long revisit to Seed of Chucky comes&nbsp;
full circle when Glen and Glenda transfer back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:47.880 --> 00:37:52.680
into the doll body from that movie, taking on&nbsp;
the new name, G/G. As another tribute to Seed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:52.680 --> 00:37:56.418
G/G has a jacket patch that resembles&nbsp;
one of the Seed of Chucky posters.

00:37:56.418 --> 00:37:59.027
One of the other patches is Tiffany's original tattoo.

00:37:59.027 --> 00:38:03.960
But the business between Chucky and the trio&nbsp;
of Jake, Devon and Lexy is not finished yet. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:03.960 --> 00:38:08.280
breaks into the house through the chimney, as&nbsp;
he has in Child’s Play and in Season 1. Also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:08.280 --> 00:38:11.760
this season began with him escaping up&nbsp;
a chimney, and now he’s coming down one.

00:38:11.760 --> 00:38:14.460
Tiffany Valentine can also be&nbsp;
found breaking into the house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:14.460 --> 00:38:18.720
looking the Belle doll to transfer her own&nbsp;
soul into, but she’s caught by Mrs. Cross.

00:38:18.720 --> 00:38:24.840
– Oh, my God. This is so random. And&nbsp;
I’m sorry to barge in on your house&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:24.840 --> 00:38:26.700
on Christmas Eve...
– Oh, no worries.

00:38:27.439 --> 00:38:31.819
– This is it? This is the&nbsp;
script we’re going with? … OK.

00:38:31.980 --> 00:38:35.940
CHUCKY Season 2 ends with one&nbsp;
final similarity to Seed. Both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:35.940 --> 00:38:38.640
stories involve Chucky breaking into&nbsp;
somewhere he’s not supposed to be,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:38.640 --> 00:38:42.180
trying to get revenge on Tiffany and&nbsp;
getting a surprise attack from a kid.

00:38:42.180 --> 00:38:45.480
Only this time, there’s another&nbsp;
twist on top of that. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:45.480 --> 00:38:50.280
it’s not a new twist. OMG Dr. Foley&nbsp;
was evil the whole time? Dr. Mixter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:50.280 --> 00:38:54.540
was evil the whole time? Caroline was evil the&nbsp;
whole time? Who could have seen this coming?

00:38:54.540 --> 00:38:58.200
I realize that I was kind of negative&nbsp;
during this episode. I usually try to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:58.200 --> 00:39:02.160
give my analysis with more of a neutral tone.&nbsp;
But it’s just hard when the characters don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:02.160 --> 00:39:05.040
make smart choices. Like why did&nbsp;
Lexy leave the chainsaw downstairs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:05.040 --> 00:39:08.160
when she knew Tiffany was still&nbsp;
upstairs? It’s just frustrating.

00:39:08.160 --> 00:39:12.840
But I do have hope. At the beginning of this&nbsp;
video, discussed how Season 1 was an homage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:12.840 --> 00:39:18.420
to Child’s Play 2 and, disappointingly, Season 2&nbsp;
falls back into the ways of Seed of Chucky. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:18.420 --> 00:39:22.980
what if that’s not necessarily the intention?&nbsp;
What if Season 1 is actually a tribute to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:22.980 --> 00:39:28.380
entire Child’s Play arc: Child’s Play, Child’s&nbsp;
Play 2, and Child’s Play 3? That would mean Season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:28.380 --> 00:39:33.000
2 is actually a tribute to the Bride-Seed&nbsp;
arc. CHUCKY has been renewed for Season 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:33.000 --> 00:39:37.560
so maybe, just maybe, Season 3 will be&nbsp;
focused on the Curse-Cult arc -- bringing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:37.560 --> 00:39:41.520
back the horror, the suspense, and the&nbsp;
psychological manipulation of the 2010s.

00:39:41.520 --> 00:39:45.240
Let me know what your thoughts are in the&nbsp;
comments. I’ll be here to cover Season 3&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:45.240 --> 00:39:49.440
once it’s available, and I’ll be updating&nbsp;
my Chucky character timelines as well. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:49.440 --> 00:39:54.060
make sure you subscribe to CZsWorld for new&nbsp;
horrors every week, RING the deathbell for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:54.060 --> 00:39:59.040
all notifications, and I will see you in&nbsp;
the next one, assuming we both survive.

00:39:59.251 --> 00:40:04.838
(spooky dance music)

